# kernel/modules/gpu/ia
#
# GPU FINAL (owner, 2026-11-03): the COMPUTE profile overlay of the gpu-ia
# entry (packages.yml, modules-only build seeded from the standard kernel
# deb). No display stack: CONFIG_DRM_AMD_DC off (the kernel-level default
# from the transverse gpu/amd.cfg fragment is overridden here, last wins),
# the HSA/KFD compute paths the ROCm runtime expects stay on, and the fb
# plumbing keeps the minimal set the base config already chose (simpledrm,
# the live installer session draws through it).
#
# The overlay merges on top of the seeded .config of the kernel deb
# (base config + the transverse kconfig-shared fragments):
#     kernel_merge_config "${SRCDIR}" kernel/modules/gpu/ia
#     make olddefconfig
#
# This file is NOT a full .config. It lists ONLY the deltas of the compute
# profile — every other value is inherited (append + olddefconfig merges).

# Display Core off: the ia build ships amdgpu without the DC display path
# (canonical unset form — olddefconfig resolves and drops the DC-only
# dependencies with it).
# CONFIG_DRM_AMD_DC is not set
# CONFIG_DRM_AMD_DC_SI is not set

# Compute: HSA userptr + SVM (the ROCm/HIP runtime paths) stay on whatever
# the display stack does.
CONFIG_HSA_AMD=y
CONFIG_HSA_AMD_SVM=y